{
  "translation": {
    "id": "BSB"
  },
  "book": {
    "id": "PSA"
  },
  "numberOfVerses": 20,
  "chapter": {
    "number": 9,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "I Will Give Thanks to the LORD"
      },
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "text": "For the choirmaster. To the tune of “The Death of the Son.” A Psalm of David."
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "text": "I will give thanks to the LORD with all my heart;\nI will recount all Your wonders.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 49,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 82,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "text": "I will be glad and rejoice in You;\nI will sing praise to Your name, O Most High.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 34,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 80,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "text": "When my enemies retreat,\nthey stumble and perish before You.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 24,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 60,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "text": "For You have upheld my just cause;\nYou sit on Your throne judging righteously.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 34,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 78,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "text": "You have rebuked the nations;\nYou have destroyed the wicked;\nYou have erased their name forever and ever.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 29,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 60,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 105,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "text": "The enemy has come to eternal ruin,\nand You have uprooted their cities;\nthe very memory of them has vanished.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 35,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 71,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 109,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "text": "But the LORD abides forever;\nHe has established His throne for judgment.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 28,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 72,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "text": "He judges the world with justice;\nHe governs the people with equity.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 33,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 68,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "text": "The LORD is a refuge for the oppressed,\na stronghold in times of trouble.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 39,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 73,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "text": "Those who know Your name trust in You,\nfor You, O LORD, have not forsaken those who seek You.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 38,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 93,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "text": "Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in Zion;\nproclaim His deeds among the nations.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 45,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 83,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "text": "For the Avenger of bloodshed remembers;\nHe does not ignore the cry of the afflicted.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 39,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 84,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "text": "Be merciful to me, O LORD;\nsee how my enemies afflict me!\nLift me up from the gates of death,",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 26,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 57,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 93,
            "level": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "text": "that I may declare all Your praises—\nthat within the gates of Daughter Zion\nI may rejoice in Your salvation.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 36,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 75,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 108,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "text": "The nations have fallen into a pit of their making;\ntheir feet are caught in the net they have hidden.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 51,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 102,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "text": "The LORD is known by the justice He brings;\nthe wicked are ensnared by the work of their hands.Higgaion Selah",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 43,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 95,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "text": "The wicked will return to Sheol—\nall the nations who forget God.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 32,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 64,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "text": "For the needy will not always be forgotten;\nnor the hope of the oppressed forever dashed.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 43,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 89,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "text": "Rise up, O LORD, do not let man prevail;\nlet the nations be judged in Your presence.",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 40,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 84,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "text": "Lay terror upon them, O LORD;\nlet the nations know they are but men.Selah",
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 29,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 68,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
